package builtin

// The functions Tack provides without a declaration. print and exit are
// extern funcs: their bodies are C, under the C names given here, and the
// compiler's code generation backend supplies those bodies for its target
// (the C backend's are in codegen/c/builtin/), so there is no Tack source
// that could be given here. A call to one is an ordinary call to its C
// function. They are available in every file without an import.
//
// This file is the documentation of record. The compiler consults
// builtin/builtin.go, and a test in that package parses this file and fails
// if the two disagree, so everything written here is true of the compiler
// beside it. Anything not yet implemented belongs in PLANNED.md instead.

// print writes s to standard output exactly as given, adding no newline.
extern("tack_builtin_print") func print(s string)

// exit ends the process immediately with the given status. Pending defers
// do not run, in the calling function or any other. Only the low bits of
// the status reach the operating system, the low 8 on Linux and macOS, so
// exit(70000) ends with status 112.
extern("tack_builtin_exit") func exit(code int64)

// len(v) returns the number of elements of the array v, or the number of
// bytes of the string v, as an int64. Its parameter takes any array or a
// string, which no Tack declaration can say, so it is described here rather
// than declared. The length of an array, and of a string literal, is a
// constant.
